@page "/privacy"
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

<PageTitle>Privacy Policy - Blocwerk</PageTitle>

<div class="legal-page">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

    <p>Last updated: June 2026</p>

    <h2>What data we collect</h2>
    <p>When you sign in via OAuth (GitHub, Google, or Microsoft), we receive and store:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Your display name</li>
        <li>Your unique account identifier from the OAuth provider</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not receive or store your email address or password.</p>

    <h2>How we use your data</h2>
    <p>Your data is used solely to identify you within the application and associate your climbing activity (attempts, boulders created, comments) with your account.</p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>We use the following cookies:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Authentication cookie</strong> &mdash; keeps you signed in for up to 8 hours</li>
        <li><strong>Antiforgery cookie</strong> &mdash; protects against cross-site request forgery</li>
        <li><strong>Cookie consent cookie</strong> &mdash; remembers that you acknowledged this notice</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not use any tracking, analytics, or advertising cookies.</p>

    <h2>Data storage</h2>
    <p>All data is stored on a self-hosted PostgreSQL database. Wall photos are stored as binary data in the database. No data is shared with third parties.</p>

